  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1209 PM MST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nWednesday and Thursday (Thanksgiving) sees tranquil conditions over \nthe Land of Enchantment as a ridge of high pressure sets up shop \nover the region Wednesday, evolving into weak flow aloft Thursday. \nHigh temperatures will range from near 50F to near 60F both days \nwith a minor cool down over eastern NM from a weak frontal boundary \nbacking southwestward from CO. \n\nFriday into the weekend places NM beneath a flattening ridge with \nweak to modest northwest flow setting up over northern NM. A weak \nshortwave disturbance embedded within this northwest flow has a \nminor risk of clipping northern and northeastern NM this weekend \nbringing light snow to the northern mountains. Otherwise, mostly dry \nand seasonal to warmer than average temperatures and breezy \nafternoons are favored most areas this weekend.",
